## Engram (knowledge-base)

**Project id:** always `knowledge-base` for `mem_search` / `mem_save` and CLI (`engram save --project knowledge-base`).

Global Memory Protocol: `~/.cursor/rules/engram.mdc`. This file is **repo-specific overlay only**.

### Division of labor (this repo)

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Audit triage, vault habits, session learnings | Engram (`mem_search` at substantive session start) |
| Symbol structure under `scripts/` | CodeGraph — `.cursor/rules/codegraph.mdc` |
| Schema, linter rules, sourcing invariants | `AGENTS.md` (read end-to-end before editing `content/`) |

### When to `mem_search` here

- Start of substantive sessions (after `AGENTS.md` if editing `content/`).
- Resuming audit tooling, vault conventions, or `effect-ts` notes.
- Examples: `audit profiles`, `vault:check`, `composer-2.5`, `effect-ts triage`, `commit policy`.

### When to `mem_save` here

- Audit profile usage (`ci` / `triage` / `full`) and default post-edit `vault:check`
- Verified triage patterns (verify high-tier findings before apply; anchor false-positive rate)
- User-stated workflow (commit only when asked; verify-first when requested)
- Tooling defaults (e.g. Composer 2.5 Fast for LLM audit passes)

Promote invariants to `AGENTS.md` + `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, not only Engram.
